(1471267, 188811, 20115, '<td valign="top">Looks like your doing pretty good with your goals for 2005.  Congratulations--beautiful shot.</td>', 'Looks like your doing pretty good with your goals for 2005.  Congratulations--beautiful shot.', '2005-06-21 13:54:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1471469, 188086, 25787, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites of the challenge.  I really love all of your bird photos.  I''m glad you were in the top ten.</td>', 'This was one of my favorites of the challenge.  I really love all of your bird photos.  I''m glad you were in the top ten.', '2005-06-21 15:41:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1471577, 188918, 8054, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon! However, I see something that bothers me and it''s the contrast between the bird and rock against the green background. It almost appears that the bird and rock were cropped out from another photo and then pasted onto the green background. I know I''m probably incorrect in that assumption but it just has that artificial feel. Regardless, looking beyond that it is a very nice and sharp photo and well done.</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon! However, I see something that bothers me and it''s the contrast between the bird and rock against the green background. It almost appears that the bird and rock were cropped out from another photo and then pasted onto the green background. I know I''m probably incorrect in that assumption but it just has that artificial feel. Regardless, looking beyond that it is a very nice and sharp photo and well done.', '2005-06-21 16:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1471625, 188811, 16301, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot, congrats!</td>', 'Excellent shot, congrats!', '2005-06-21 16:57:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1471627, 188755, 7743, '<td valign="top">I scored this a 7 but here''s what I see...<br/> <br/>- Foreground feathers seem to be over exposed<br/>- Feathers around the top of the head are out of focus and the eyelid seems to be a bit soft.  This may be due to movement of the bird indicating that a faster shutter speed should have been used.<br/> <br/>The DOF could be increased therefore bringing more of the bird into focus.</td>', 'I scored this a 7 but here''s what I see... - Foreground feathers seem to be over exposed- Feathers around the top of the head are out of focus and the eyelid seems to be a bit soft.  This may be due to movement of the bird indicating that a faster shutter speed should have been used. The DOF could be increased therefore bringing more of the bird into focus.', '2005-06-21 16:59:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1472155, 188668, 6306, '<td valign="top">I don''t like this. It looks like the swan is drooling.  Not a flattering portrait of such a graceful animal.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-21 21:39:14.</i></td>', 'I don''t like this. It looks like the swan is drooling.  Not a flattering portrait of such a graceful animal.', '2005-06-21 22:39:00.000000', '2005-06-21 22:39:14.000000', 0),
(1472166, 188668, 30791, '<td valign="top">create a print!</td>', 'create a print!', '2005-06-21 22:43:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1472308, 188811, 92, '<td valign="top">Well deserved Blue ribbon ! The clarity and compostion are spot on !</td>', 'Well deserved Blue ribbon ! The clarity and compostion are spot on !', '2005-06-21 23:27:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474111, 188811, 7543, '<td valign="top">Magnað, til hamingju <br/> <br/>Tyrkinn<br/> <br/>(Amazing, congrats)</td>', 'Magnað, til hamingju  Tyrkinn (Amazing, congrats)', '2005-06-22 09:58:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474114, 188811, 2130, '<td valign="top">frábær mynd...geggjuð dýpt og litir, til lukku með borðann :)</td>', 'frábær mynd...geggjuð dýpt og litir, til lukku með borðann :)', '2005-06-22 09:59:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474176, 188315, 36078, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club<br/> <br/>The shot to me seems a bit unbalanced.   The space above the ducklings seems to be wasted and with a undeatiled foreground it is more emphasized.  On the left of the mother duck the reed/roots seems bit over exposed and competing against the foregrounds colors. <br/> <br/>I do think the colors are very nice overall.  If you were able to move further to the left and include more of the ducklings without so much of the foreground it would have improved your shot.  The muddy water does not seem to pick up the reflection enough.  Maybe it is from a product of noise reduction.<br/> <br/>The border does not really work for me either.  I do not care for the green and thought maybe a simple black or white thin border would have been better.  <br/> <br/>Overall a nice piece to get back into the swing of things.  Looking forward to seeing more of your work.</td>', 'From Critique Club The shot to me seems a bit unbalanced.   The space above the ducklings seems to be wasted and with a undeatiled foreground it is more emphasized.  On the left of the mother duck the reed/roots seems bit over exposed and competing against the foregrounds colors.  I do think the colors are very nice overall.  If you were able to move further to the left and include more of the ducklings without so much of the foreground it would have improved your shot.  The muddy water does not seem to pick up the reflection enough.  Maybe it is from a product of noise reduction. The border does not really work for me either.  I do not care for the green and thought maybe a simple black or white thin border would have been better.   Overall a nice piece to get back into the swing of things.  Looking forward to seeing more of your work.', '2005-06-22 10:21:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474257, 187680, 36078, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club<br/> <br/>The motion blur of the wings is very striking at first.  But with this style it leaves out alot of detail in the face and wings.  I am not saying either is wrong.  Just two different styles to approach.  <br/> <br/>The grass to me has a bluish tint and under exposed.  I do find the colors and contrast to be refreshing and spot on.  The legs seem a bit odd to me.  <br/> <br/>The overall placement is well balanced.  The viewer sees the main subject without having anything competeing with it.  I also like the lack of a border.  I do not have anything against borders but find you really did not need one.</td>', 'From Critique Club The motion blur of the wings is very striking at first.  But with this style it leaves out alot of detail in the face and wings.  I am not saying either is wrong.  Just two different styles to approach.   The grass to me has a bluish tint and under exposed.  I do find the colors and contrast to be refreshing and spot on.  The legs seem a bit odd to me.   The overall placement is well balanced.  The viewer sees the main subject without having anything competeing with it.  I also like the lack of a border.  I do not have anything against borders but find you really did not need one.', '2005-06-22 10:39:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474472, 188615, 36078, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club<br/> <br/>I find the image to be very pleasing and very nostalgic.  The muddled background colors blend very well.  I think the image is well balanced from top to bottom but not side to side. I would have liked to see the main bird more in the center of the image.  <br/> <br/>I am not sure why the image scored the way it did.  I found it to stand out against the zoomed in closeups of birds at a zoo.<br/> <br/>I think the border is a bit wide but only slightly...with the whiteness of the cord/string the birds seem to sit in the image if that makes sense.</td>', 'From Critique Club I find the image to be very pleasing and very nostalgic.  The muddled background colors blend very well.  I think the image is well balanced from top to bottom but not side to side. I would have liked to see the main bird more in the center of the image.   I am not sure why the image scored the way it did.  I found it to stand out against the zoomed in closeups of birds at a zoo. I think the border is a bit wide but only slightly...with the whiteness of the cord/string the birds seem to sit in the image if that makes sense.', '2005-06-22 11:22:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474698, 188811, 24841, '<td valign="top">Perfect!</td>', 'Perfect!', '2005-06-22 12:21:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474710, 187043, 24841, '<td valign="top">Nice and neat...lovely!</td>', 'Nice and neat...lovely!', '2005-06-22 12:25:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474714, 189068, 24841, '<td valign="top">Wicked, the color is spectacular!</td>', 'Wicked, the color is spectacular!', '2005-06-22 12:26:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474965, 188798, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Nice bird, does not seem out of focus but lack detail on the feathers and head, probrably from USM.  Highlights and colors are fine.  The background makes the image seem a bit darker to me then it probrably is.<br/> <br/>The way you cropped it emphasizes the tilt the bird has.  Maybe a bit more room on the left would have helped in that area.<br/> <br/>I like the scale of the bird, I think you had the right idea just some unknown sharpening issues.<br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club Nice bird, does not seem out of focus but lack detail on the feathers and head, probrably from USM.  Highlights and colors are fine.  The background makes the image seem a bit darker to me then it probrably is. The way you cropped it emphasizes the tilt the bird has.  Maybe a bit more room on the left would have helped in that area. I like the scale of the bird, I think you had the right idea just some unknown sharpening issues.', '2005-06-22 13:24:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475018, 188755, 36078, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club<br/> <br/>I find the bottom center feathers a bit overexposed.  I do not know if it was a result of some other factor or in the original image.  it does not detract to much but almost appears fake to me.<br/> <br/>Lots of detail in the face but for some reason the eye seems a bit soft in focus.  Might just be the angle or some post preocessing artifact.<br/> <br/>Nice scale to the overall bird.  Does not compete with the background for the viewers attention.  The border works well...nice size and enough thickness.</td>', 'From Critique Club I find the bottom center feathers a bit overexposed.  I do not know if it was a result of some other factor or in the original image.  it does not detract to much but almost appears fake to me. Lots of detail in the face but for some reason the eye seems a bit soft in focus.  Might just be the angle or some post preocessing artifact. Nice scale to the overall bird.  Does not compete with the background for the viewers attention.  The border works well...nice size and enough thickness.', '2005-06-22 13:35:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475055, 187953, 36078, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club<br/> <br/>I like the scale of the glass birds.  I do find the sky as a background to distract from the overall color of the birds.  If something a bit darker was used it would have also taken the reflections and bubbles from inside of the glass.<br/> <br/>I like the concept and the blue of the birds.  The angle seems fine but maybe a more level head on shot would have worked better.<br/> <br/>The border is fine but I do not think you really needed a border.</td>', 'From Critique Club I like the scale of the glass birds.  I do find the sky as a background to distract from the overall color of the birds.  If something a bit darker was used it would have also taken the reflections and bubbles from inside of the glass. I like the concept and the blue of the birds.  The angle seems fine but maybe a more level head on shot would have worked better. The border is fine but I do not think you really needed a border.', '2005-06-22 13:43:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475149, 188919, 36078, '<td valign="top">From Critique Club<br/> <br/>I find the overall image a bit small.  It is difficult to capture birds at times.   And you have to work hard at it.  <br/> <br/>I love the pose....very nicely captured.  I find the contrast a bit on the weak side.  But with a black almost colorless bird it is hard to boost anything up.  <br/> <br/>The noise in the blackness detracts and makes the soft focus appear worse.  The background is fine but would have been a bit better to have gotten it on a smooth more eye appealing texture.<br/> <br/>I think you are on the right track and with help the image coul dhave been better.</td>', 'From Critique Club I find the overall image a bit small.  It is difficult to capture birds at times.   And you have to work hard at it.   I love the pose....very nicely captured.  I find the contrast a bit on the weak side.  But with a black almost colorless bird it is hard to boost anything up.   The noise in the blackness detracts and makes the soft focus appear worse.  The background is fine but would have been a bit better to have gotten it on a smooth more eye appealing texture. I think you are on the right track and with help the image coul dhave been better.', '2005-06-22 14:03:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475453, 189010, 29177, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gaia:</b></div><hr/><i> wow. Only two comments and average score of 4.98.  I really enjoyed this picture. I would have liked to hear why so many people decided to vote 3 to 5 points. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m stumped too Cathy..... sigh</td>', 'Originally posted by Gaia: wow. Only two comments and average score of 4.98.  I really enjoyed this picture. I would have liked to hear why so many people decided to vote 3 to 5 points.   I''m stumped too Cathy..... sigh', '2005-06-22 15:18:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475468, 187209, 34247, '<td valign="top">Wonderful subject, dof and coloration. Quite an eye to get this right. The crop is a good one too, and I really like the title as well :)</td>', 'Wonderful subject, dof and coloration. Quite an eye to get this right. The crop is a good one too, and I really like the title as well :)', '2005-06-22 15:21:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475632, 189039, 34659, '<td valign="top">* Greetings from the Critique Club *<br/> <br/>First of all, nice image.  I really like the muted tones &amp; blues.<br/> <br/>I think you could have cropped it a little more to emphasize the subjects more attractively.  As it currently stands, I think there''s too much negative space that''s not working in your favor for this particular image.  Also, the image is a bit too dark - you''re losing a lot of the detail that could really enhance this image (especially given different monitor respresentations that don''t always portray dark images with the contrast you may see on your own monitor).<br/> <br/>I think the composition could be improved with a slightly different crop.  As I said, I really like the color choices - muted blue tones really add a nice, peaceful, and somewhat animalistic appeal to the shot.  I also think that if the birds were actually closer, it would have more appeal and you could really capitalize on DOF.  As it is, you are limited on the amount of focus you can really bring out in this image.  Perhaps you were going for something more along these lines, however.  If so, I think that the crop again could be utilized more effectively.<br/> <br/>I remember this image from the Birds Challenge.  If I recall, I believe I scored it a 5.  I thought that it certainly met the challenge, but that the overall impression I got from the image was not what it could be.  It just didn''t hold my attention...  (Sorry)<br/> <br/>Again too, it''s YOUR impression and opinion that matters most when reviewing your work - not someone who is less knowledgeable of the intent of your photograph.  You might want to include some notes of your own in the photos you want critiqued, because that gives us a little more to go on when we''re providing feedback.<br/> <br/>All in all, it''s a solid image and as I said, I like the understated blue tones.  You''ve established a nice mood, I just think you could improve the actual execution and presentation of your piece (with some more post-processing work).<br/> <br/>Just my 2 cents...<br/> <br/>Jimmy<br/></td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club * First of all, nice image.  I really like the muted tones & blues. I think you could have cropped it a little more to emphasize the subjects more attractively.  As it currently stands, I think there''s too much negative space that''s not working in your favor for this particular image.  Also, the image is a bit too dark - you''re losing a lot of the detail that could really enhance this image (especially given different monitor respresentations that don''t always portray dark images with the contrast you may see on your own monitor). I think the composition could be improved with a slightly different crop.  As I said, I really like the color choices - muted blue tones really add a nice, peaceful, and somewhat animalistic appeal to the shot.  I also think that if the birds were actually closer, it would have more appeal and you could really capitalize on DOF.  As it is, you are limited on the amount of focus you can really bring out in this image.  Perhaps you were going for something more along these lines, however.  If so, I think that the crop again could be utilized more effectively. I remember this image from the Birds Challenge.  If I recall, I believe I scored it a 5.  I thought that it certainly met the challenge, but that the overall impression I got from the image was not what it could be.  It just didn''t hold my attention...  (Sorry) Again too, it''s YOUR impression and opinion that matters most when reviewing your work - not someone who is less knowledgeable of the intent of your photograph.  You might want to include some notes of your own in the photos you want critiqued, because that gives us a little more to go on when we''re providing feedback. All in all, it''s a solid image and as I said, I like the understated blue tones.  You''ve established a nice mood, I just think you could improve the actual execution and presentation of your piece (with some more post-processing work). Just my 2 cents... Jimmy', '2005-06-22 16:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475645, 188122, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Stunning image, very well balanced.  Nice tones and detail in the birds and textures.  I do find the twigs/branches in the upper right corner a bit distracting.<br/> <br/>I personally do not like the bamboo/cane/vine splitting the 2 birds.  But I could see where others would welcome it.<br/> <br/>The background seems a bit muddled but nothing you could have done about it.  Overall a powerful image with what has become of our national birds.  A closer crop or zoom might have gained it some points.</td>', 'From the Critique Club Stunning image, very well balanced.  Nice tones and detail in the birds and textures.  I do find the twigs/branches in the upper right corner a bit distracting. I personally do not like the bamboo/cane/vine splitting the 2 birds.  But I could see where others would welcome it. The background seems a bit muddled but nothing you could have done about it.  Overall a powerful image with what has become of our national birds.  A closer crop or zoom might have gained it some points.', '2005-06-22 16:32:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475673, 187565, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very striking image, great mood and depth to the photo.  Everything is beautifully detailed.  I do find the tree limb to be a bit lackluster.  I do not mind the business of the background.  it does compete with the colors of the bird somewhat but not displeasing.<br/> <br/>Nicely proportioned and centered well.  I am not sure why the image did not do better.  The border is nice and distracting.  Probably came down to personal taste and you can never please everyone.</td>', 'From the Critique Club Very striking image, great mood and depth to the photo.  Everything is beautifully detailed.  I do find the tree limb to be a bit lackluster.  I do not mind the business of the background.  it does compete with the colors of the bird somewhat but not displeasing. Nicely proportioned and centered well.  I am not sure why the image did not do better.  The border is nice and distracting.  Probably came down to personal taste and you can never please everyone.', '2005-06-22 16:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475740, 187224, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Striking pose, fills the frame nicely.  Maybe a bit to cropped off on top, just by a hair.  Great detail in the hair,face and beak.<br/> <br/>I think what may have hurt the image was opinions it was an ugly and beat up looking bird.  I still find it very pleasing and not in that sort of mood.<br/> <br/>I think the fence frames the bird nicely but a little more clarity might have given more emphasis with that.</td>', 'From the Critique Club Striking pose, fills the frame nicely.  Maybe a bit to cropped off on top, just by a hair.  Great detail in the hair,face and beak. I think what may have hurt the image was opinions it was an ugly and beat up looking bird.  I still find it very pleasing and not in that sort of mood. I think the fence frames the bird nicely but a little more clarity might have given more emphasis with that.', '2005-06-22 17:01:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475829, 187043, 24744, '<td valign="top">Nice lens ;)</td>', 'Nice lens ;)', '2005-06-22 17:23:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475867, 189074, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rktdesign:</b></div><hr/><i> LOVE the comp and DOF of this image...I also really like the super limited color pallette..that eye is perfect! ...really nicely done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks!<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by amber:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the ggraphic quality of this image. With the bird sitting up above too it reminds me of Hitchcock''s ''the birds'' :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yeah, that''s the idea, or maybe Poe''s raven. I only got part of the bird partly because he was not very cooperative about sitting still, and I wanted to use one in-focus : )</td>', 'Originally posted by rktdesign: LOVE the comp and DOF of this image...I also really like the super limited color pallette..that eye is perfect! ...really nicely done.  Thanks!Originally posted by amber: I like the ggraphic quality of this image. With the bird sitting up above too it reminds me of Hitchcock''s ''the birds'' :)  Yeah, that''s the idea, or maybe Poe''s raven. I only got part of the bird partly because he was not very cooperative about sitting still, and I wanted to use one in-focus : )', '2005-06-22 17:34:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476013, 187284, 1717, '<td valign="top">wow...outstanding capture!  my yard is always full of red wing blackbirds and i love watching them and listening to them.  love your composition here and the focus is spot on.  well done, John!</td>', 'wow...outstanding capture!  my yard is always full of red wing blackbirds and i love watching them and listening to them.  love your composition here and the focus is spot on.  well done, John!', '2005-06-22 18:03:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476200, 187043, 22734, '<td valign="top">From the critique club:<br/> <br/>Are you kidding? I doubt that anyone can improve on this lovely image. The true charm lies with cute subject and its heartwarming expression. The perching is outstanding. The composition is complete and very well cropped.<br/> <br/>As is, it is complete. Wise selection of dof to obliterate the background. The pole and its color becomes the leading support and to find its tiny talons embracing its adds charm.<br/> <br/>While this image is complete there is also the alternative takes by zooming in closer, but then this becomes a different image.<br/> <br/>The colors are pleasing and the image does not suffer from over sharpenning. All in all, I expected this image in the top 5. 11th is good because the competition is real hot in this challenge, so hot that I was happy with my sparrow score. Top twenty, as in your case, means that the image is above average. Your technique, as displayed is very promising and you have a very good eye and good taste. Now, get out of here and keep up the nice work.</td>', 'From the critique club: Are you kidding? I doubt that anyone can improve on this lovely image. The true charm lies with cute subject and its heartwarming expression. The perching is outstanding. The composition is complete and very well cropped. As is, it is complete. Wise selection of dof to obliterate the background. The pole and its color becomes the leading support and to find its tiny talons embracing its adds charm. While this image is complete there is also the alternative takes by zooming in closer, but then this becomes a different image. The colors are pleasing and the image does not suffer from over sharpenning. All in all, I expected this image in the top 5. 11th is good because the competition is real hot in this challenge, so hot that I was happy with my sparrow score. Top twenty, as in your case, means that the image is above average. Your technique, as displayed is very promising and you have a very good eye and good taste. Now, get out of here and keep up the nice work.', '2005-06-22 18:42:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476376, 189069, 32997, '<td valign="top">i think this is the best shot from this challenge..there is life here, and wonderful context..your timing is perfect, levels spot on...the reflections that result from the angle are wonderful..and the thing that i don''t quite get..this shot hits me emotionally and i don''t particularily like birds, avoided the challenge..scanning through saw this and am taken with it..you have a wonderful eye for composition!</td>', 'i think this is the best shot from this challenge..there is life here, and wonderful context..your timing is perfect, levels spot on...the reflections that result from the angle are wonderful..and the thing that i don''t quite get..this shot hits me emotionally and i don''t particularily like birds, avoided the challenge..scanning through saw this and am taken with it..you have a wonderful eye for composition!', '2005-06-22 19:24:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1477511, 188811, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''m very happy this won; I love those birds, and I love the pure, intricate detail of this shot. Add in that there''s something startlingly human about this bird''s "expression", and you managed to capture the hearts of the voters with a very simple, disarmingly simple, image. Congrats!</td>', 'I''m very happy this won; I love those birds, and I love the pure, intricate detail of this shot. Add in that there''s something startlingly human about this bird''s "expression", and you managed to capture the hearts of the voters with a very simple, disarmingly simple, image. Congrats!', '2005-06-23 03:15:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1477514, 188918, 30861, '<td valign="top">Simply gorgeous. The purity of the BG is marvelous, it''s a living color and it is startling in its power. The "pose", of course, is to die for. Nice work!</td>', 'Simply gorgeous. The purity of the BG is marvelous, it''s a living color and it is startling in its power. The "pose", of course, is to die for. Nice work!', '2005-06-23 03:17:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1477830, 188982, 38522, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for your comments. This was my first challenge and I have learned a lot so far. I had a feeling I was going to get more negative feedback but I am happy with my score and everyones helpful remarks.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for your comments. This was my first challenge and I have learned a lot so far. I had a feeling I was going to get more negative feedback but I am happy with my score and everyones helpful remarks.', '2005-06-23 09:47:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1477843, 186660, 25355, '<td valign="top">Well, I never would say that emus are an ugly bird, maybe more "interesting" than pretty, but certainly not ugly (well, okay - they''re ugly after being hit by a semitrailer in the Outback with feathers strewn all over the place). Good shot, anyway, Glen. I wish I''d had time to bump it up, but at least you got a vote from me.</td>', 'Well, I never would say that emus are an ugly bird, maybe more "interesting" than pretty, but certainly not ugly (well, okay - they''re ugly after being hit by a semitrailer in the Outback with feathers strewn all over the place). Good shot, anyway, Glen. I wish I''d had time to bump it up, but at least you got a vote from me.', '2005-06-23 09:54:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1477913, 188668, 38223, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ErikaS:</b></div><hr/><i> How did this not win first place? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s the drool</td>', 'Originally posted by ErikaS: How did this not win first place?   It''s the drool', '2005-06-23 10:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478100, 189062, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Right off the image seems a little soft on focus.  I do find the image very well put together beides that.  Proportions are well balanced.  <br/> <br/>Their is a but of a blurry highlight(for a lack of a better word) on the background right in front of the birds beak.  I think the colors need a little pop but with added detail of it being slightly more in focus it could have solved the problem.<br/> <br/>The lighting seems to be behind the bird and on the right.  The side you photographed just does not pick up any of the light besides the crown of his head.<br/> <br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club Right off the image seems a little soft on focus.  I do find the image very well put together beides that.  Proportions are well balanced.   Their is a but of a blurry highlight(for a lack of a better word) on the background right in front of the birds beak.  I think the colors need a little pop but with added detail of it being slightly more in focus it could have solved the problem. The lighting seems to be behind the bird and on the right.  The side you photographed just does not pick up any of the light besides the crown of his head. ', '2005-06-23 11:55:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478158, 187902, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I think either a closer zoom or closer crop would have worked better.  Being darker colored birds on pretty dark water they tend to be hidden.<br/> <br/>The left tree leaves are a bit distracting. The coloring seems find for what colors are present but the lack of any detail overall hurts the image.  <br/> <br/>The framing to be is a bit off as well.  The leaves on open side then the birds then the boulder.  It does draw the viewers eye right across all of that in a diagonal line.  But the birds get overlooked.</td>', 'From the Critique Club I think either a closer zoom or closer crop would have worked better.  Being darker colored birds on pretty dark water they tend to be hidden. The left tree leaves are a bit distracting. The coloring seems find for what colors are present but the lack of any detail overall hurts the image.   The framing to be is a bit off as well.  The leaves on open side then the birds then the boulder.  It does draw the viewers eye right across all of that in a diagonal line.  But the birds get overlooked.', '2005-06-23 12:15:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478212, 188826, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very striking image.  Very nicely detailed, well put together.  Fills the frame nicely and the background does not compete with the subject.  The background does has a weir horizontal line but I am sure you could not change it.<br/> <br/>Very nice expression on the face/eyes/beak.  I do find their to be some noise on the entire image.  Nothing that hurt it because I personally do not mind it on the entire image.  it does give the image a nostalgic look and feel to it.<br/> <br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club Very striking image.  Very nicely detailed, well put together.  Fills the frame nicely and the background does not compete with the subject.  The background does has a weir horizontal line but I am sure you could not change it. Very nice expression on the face/eyes/beak.  I do find their to be some noise on the entire image.  Nothing that hurt it because I personally do not mind it on the entire image.  it does give the image a nostalgic look and feel to it. ', '2005-06-23 12:33:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478253, 187148, 35161, '<td valign="top">One of my fav. for this challenge! <br/>Nice once again! :)</td>', 'One of my fav. for this challenge! Nice once again! :)', '2005-06-23 12:48:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478639, 188918, 332, '<td valign="top">Shooting with 400mm F/2.8 and 1.4x extender you get 560mm and I took it at  F/6.3 you will get this effect :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MrAkamai:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on your ribbon! However, I see something that bothers me and it''s the contrast between the bird and rock against the green background. It almost appears that the bird and rock were cropped out from another photo and then pasted onto the green background. I know I''m probably incorrect in that assumption but it just has that artificial feel. Regardless, looking beyond that it is a very nice and sharp photo and well done. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Shooting with 400mm F/2.8 and 1.4x extender you get 560mm and I took it at  F/6.3 you will get this effect :) Originally posted by MrAkamai: Congratulations on your ribbon! However, I see something that bothers me and it''s the contrast between the bird and rock against the green background. It almost appears that the bird and rock were cropped out from another photo and then pasted onto the green background. I know I''m probably incorrect in that assumption but it just has that artificial feel. Regardless, looking beyond that it is a very nice and sharp photo and well done. ', '2005-06-23 14:51:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1479212, 186959, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very classic looking photo of a swan.  To me for being as close as the subject seems to be the lack of detail.  Their are some nice details in the neck/head but none in the eye beak area.  The bird is pretty white on the tail end and that may not make for very much detail.  <br/> <br/>The water is nicely colored without being harsh or to busy.  I would have preferred the photo to be cropped with more room on the right and more of the reflection.<br/> <br/>The bird has the right size to fill the frame. And still draws the viewers attention.</td>', 'From the Critique Club Very classic looking photo of a swan.  To me for being as close as the subject seems to be the lack of detail.  Their are some nice details in the neck/head but none in the eye beak area.  The bird is pretty white on the tail end and that may not make for very much detail.   The water is nicely colored without being harsh or to busy.  I would have preferred the photo to be cropped with more room on the right and more of the reflection. The bird has the right size to fill the frame. And still draws the viewers attention.', '2005-06-23 18:07:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1479800, 188776, 32033, '<td valign="top">Thanks very much for comments</td>', 'Thanks very much for comments', '2005-06-23 22:14:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1479896, 187644, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very strking pose, the smoothness of the front/wings makes it looks fake in some way.  But not in a negative way.  I like the framing of the bird on the right.  Enough room between the side and the bird and then space to the right.<br/> <br/>Very high quality photo.  Nice color and brightness.  Nothing to overpowering.  Only thing I personally find a little distracting is the background.  It goes from dark to light.  Some may like it but I had to really search for something I did not like about this photo.<br/> <br/>I think it is a great capture and not sure why it did not place higher.</td>', 'From the Critique Club Very strking pose, the smoothness of the front/wings makes it looks fake in some way.  But not in a negative way.  I like the framing of the bird on the right.  Enough room between the side and the bird and then space to the right. Very high quality photo.  Nice color and brightness.  Nothing to overpowering.  Only thing I personally find a little distracting is the background.  It goes from dark to light.  Some may like it but I had to really search for something I did not like about this photo. I think it is a great capture and not sure why it did not place higher.', '2005-06-23 22:52:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1479987, 188727, 33515, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comment <br/> <br/>Composition: <br/> <br/>When I first view this image I am drawn to the negative space to the left and away from the bird and lamp post to focus on the winged figure. I then spend more time trying to figure out just what it is and lose touch with the real subject, the bird on the lamp post. I really like your subject, the bird staring at you as you take its picture and the crack in the glass adds to the scene. If you could have positioned yourself to take advantage of the cracked glass and light the birds neck for more detail I feel you would have improved on your score. <br/> <br/>Background: <br/> <br/>The background is a bit busy and draws you away from the subject. I find the building very interesting and its light colors helps your mainly black foreground stand out. Again changing position away for the figure may have helped here. I see the connection between the statue and Birds challenge, but to me it is too much of a distraction.<br/> <br/>Camera Work: <br/> <br/>The focus and DOF make this image stand out; your subject really pops off the page. The high ISO may add to a bit of softness in the top of the lamp post. <br/> <br/>Post-Processing: <br/> <br/>I noticed you didnt take full advantage of the 150kb file size which could have added more detail as well as using UMS if shooting RAW. I am not big on a lot of post processing and always find restraint a refreshing change. The boarder is a nice size and really helps frame your image.<br/> <br/> <br/>My Opinion: <br/> <br/>Personally, I feel that this shot with a few changes has great potential. The composition doesn''t hit the mark, for me anyway, so I''d rate this as an average to above average shot. <br/> <br/>This photo meets the challenge, in my opinion, but the background draws too much attention. I feel this lead to your slightly below average score (5.488 for this challenge) and after viewing your portfolio maybe slight disappointment on your part. <br/> <br/>This is one of my first critiques and I hope you find it helpful. Just as you are looking for some help from the Critique Club I would enjoy any feed back you have to improve myself. If you have any comments or questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment  Composition:  When I first view this image I am drawn to the negative space to the left and away from the bird and lamp post to focus on the winged figure. I then spend more time trying to figure out just what it is and lose touch with the real subject, the bird on the lamp post. I really like your subject, the bird staring at you as you take its picture and the crack in the glass adds to the scene. If you could have positioned yourself to take advantage of the cracked glass and light the birds neck for more detail I feel you would have improved on your score.  Background:  The background is a bit busy and draws you away from the subject. I find the building very interesting and its light colors helps your mainly black foreground stand out. Again changing position away for the figure may have helped here. I see the connection between the statue and Birds challenge, but to me it is too much of a distraction. Camera Work:  The focus and DOF make this image stand out; your subject really pops off the page. The high ISO may add to a bit of softness in the top of the lamp post.  Post-Processing:  I noticed you didnt take full advantage of the 150kb file size which could have added more detail as well as using UMS if shooting RAW. I am not big on a lot of post processing and always find restraint a refreshing change. The boarder is a nice size and really helps frame your image.  My Opinion:  Personally, I feel that this shot with a few changes has great potential. The composition doesn''t hit the mark, for me anyway, so I''d rate this as an average to above average shot.  This photo meets the challenge, in my opinion, but the background draws too much attention. I feel this lead to your slightly below average score (5.488 for this challenge) and after viewing your portfolio maybe slight disappointment on your part.  This is one of my first critiques and I hope you find it helpful. Just as you are looking for some help from the Critique Club I would enjoy any feed back you have to improve myself. If you have any comments or questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.', '2005-06-23 23:39:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1480539, 188915, 6630, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>   Composition:<br/> <br/>The subject is a little too centered for my liking and the tree trunk on the right side is a bit distracting and takes the attention away from the main subject.  I think a tighter crop would have worked better here.<br/> <br/>   Background:<br/> <br/>The background is perfect for this subject and compliments it very well.  I like the bokeh and the way it contrasts against the foreground without being distracting.<br/> <br/>  My opinion:<br/> <br/>I would have personally given this picture a 6.  It meets the challenge just fine but I am not crazy about the crop.  I like the colors and the subject but I really would have liked to see more of the bird and less of the surroundings.  Perhaps the bird''s head filling the frame would have had a much stonger impact.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions or comments on this critique, please feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>June<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!    Composition: The subject is a little too centered for my liking and the tree trunk on the right side is a bit distracting and takes the attention away from the main subject.  I think a tighter crop would have worked better here.    Background: The background is perfect for this subject and compliments it very well.  I like the bokeh and the way it contrasts against the foreground without being distracting.   My opinion: I would have personally given this picture a 6.  It meets the challenge just fine but I am not crazy about the crop.  I like the colors and the subject but I really would have liked to see more of the bird and less of the surroundings.  Perhaps the bird''s head filling the frame would have had a much stonger impact. If you have any questions or comments on this critique, please feel free to PM me. June ', '2005-06-24 07:22:41.000000', NULL, 0),
